# Design system fidelity (Exactera)

- **Always read `system.md` at repo root** before building or changing UI, styling, prototypes, tokens, typography, spacing, brand usage, or new design-system-aligned components.
- **Do not invent** fonts, hex values, palettes, semantic color names, typography scales (sizes, weights, spacing, radii), or component conventions that are absent from **`system.md`** (foundations/tokens) or from the **component source file** paths **`system.md`** points to—unless the user clearly authorizes a new convention **and** you update **`system.md`** (paths/registry) and the **component file** (definitions) when applicable.
- **Do not substitute arbitrary values** (“close enough” colors, eyeballed rem, unofficial weights) where **`system.md`**, linked component sources, or implementations define controlled values.
- If requirements conflict with **`system.md`**, are ambiguous, or the spec does not yet cover something you need (**ask the user** for clarification rather than improvising).

When in doubt: **pause and ask.**
